 FR1–FR17 and user stories 1–16 (sign in, reset password, service buttons with status, printable papers, PDF/PNG/JPG upload,
 staff add/edit/search students, additional fees, approve/reject with reason, meetings, email-notification log, fees report + CSV).
 Emails are simulated (shown in notifications / "Email sent"); passwords are plain text only inside the mock.
+
+## Printing (real backend)
+`#/staff/print` ("Print papers", staff only) is the first page wired to a real server, via `js/printing.js` + `css/printing.css`.
+It lists students from the database, lets staff pick a template and generates a print-ready paper on the server
+(`GET /api/templates`, `GET /api/students`, `GET /print/{studentId}/{templateCode}`). Every print is logged in `print_log`.
+Open the portal through the .NET app (`http://localhost:5080`), not from `file://`, so those paths resolve.
+Until portal sign-in uses the backend, the page asks for a printing key and a staff user id (temporary; see the header of `js/printing.js`).
+The student "Print paper" buttons still use the client-side mock (`printPaper()` in `ui.js`): the server cannot yet know which student is signed in.
